# Line endings - everything is stored AND checked out as LF.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` in the global git config on the development
# machines, so every `git checkout`, `stash pop` and `reset --hard` wrote CRLF
# back into the working tree. That is what gave Maintain/Format.sh's line-ending
# pass work to do on a tree that had just been converted, and it is the reason
# the pass existed at all (t_6b9a495a).
#
# A repository attribute outranks a user-level `core.autocrlf`, so this holds
# for any clone on any machine, whatever its git config says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary - never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
